"<!-- cngx:generated 1b842b43 -->
<!-- ng-add, @cngx 0.1.0 -->

# cngx in this project

\`ng add\` set up cngx 0.1.0 here and wrote this file. A later \`ng add\`
run regenerates it, so edits made here are not kept.

## Installed

- \`@cngx/utils@0.1.0\`
- \`@cngx/core@0.1.0\`
- \`@cngx/common@0.1.0\`
- \`@cngx/interop@0.1.0\`
- \`@cngx/forms@0.1.0\`
- \`@cngx/data-display@0.1.0\`
- \`@cngx/ui@0.1.0\`
- \`@cngx/themes@0.1.0\`

## MCP server

Your coding agent asks the \`cngx\` MCP server (\`@cngx/mcp@0.3.0\`)
about components, inputs, slots, theme tokens and DI tokens instead of
guessing them. It runs locally through \`npx\`, answers offline from the cngx
API snapshot it bundles, and needs no account or key.

Configured in:

- \`.mcp.json\`
- \`.vscode/mcp.json\`
- \`AGENTS.md\`

### Tools

| Tool | What it answers | Try asking |
|-|-|-|
| \`find_component\` | Find cngx component, directive, or service | Which cngx component renders a searchable single select? |
| \`get_api\` | Get cngx component API | What inputs and outputs does CngxSelect take? |
| \`get_config\` | Get a cngx configuration cascade | How do I set app-wide defaults for CngxSelect? |
| \`get_di_tokens\` | Get cngx DI tokens | Which DI tokens configure the select family? |
| \`get_slots\` | Get cngx component template slots | Which template slots can I override on CngxSelect? |
| \`get_story_example\` | Get cngx example URLs | Show me a working example of CngxTreeSelect. |
| \`get_theme_tokens\` | Get cngx component theming tokens | Which custom properties theme CngxChip? |
| \`list_components\` | List cngx components, directives, and services | Which directives does @cngx/common ship? |
| \`migrate_usage\` | Diff two cngx releases | What breaks between cngx 0.1.0-rc.5 and 0.1.0? |

### Resources

| URI | Content |
|-|-|
| \`cngx://catalog\` | Every cngx component, directive, and injectable service as { name, kind, selector, category, lib }, sorted by name. The browse view of list_components. |
| \`cngx://tokens\` | The top-level DI injection tokens as { name, file, description }. |
| \`cngx://provenance\` | Snapshot meta: cngx version, generatedAt, schemaVersion, compodocx version. |
| \`cngx://api/{name}\` | One component or directive's API surface (inputs, outputs, signal flag, host bindings, methods) by class name or selector. An unknown name yields an empty resource. |
| \`cngx://llms\` | The llms.txt-equivalent entry index - documented-exports counts, API-reference pointer links and the package list - composed offline from the bundled snapshot. |
| \`cngx://llms-full\` | The verbatim compodocx llm-md dump - the full API export with every artifact's selector, inputs, outputs, description and live-example URLs - served offline from the bundled snapshot. The companion to the cngx://llms index; an absent dump yields an empty resource. |

### Prompts

| Prompt | Use |
|-|-|
| \`wire_component\` | Frame wiring one cngx component and name the tools to ground against. |
| \`theme_component\` | Frame theming one cngx component through its exposed custom properties. |
| \`migrate_cngx\` | Frame a cross-version cngx migration grounded in migrate_usage. |

## Check that it runs

- Claude Code: run \`claude mcp list\` in this folder; \`cngx\` is listed once you approve the project server.
- VS Code: run \`MCP: List Servers\` from the command palette and start \`cngx\`.

## Turn it off

Delete the \`cngx\` entry from each config file listed above, and the block
between \`<!-- cngx:agents -->\` and \`<!-- /cngx:agents -->\` in \`AGENTS.md\`.
Nothing else in the project depends on the server.

## Clients outside this project

\`ng add\` writes only project files. To use the server in Claude Desktop or
in every Cursor project, add the same entry to that client's own config by
hand (\`claude_desktop_config.json\`, \`~/.cursor/mcp.json\`):

\`\`\`json
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "cngx": { "command": "npx", "args": ["-y", "@cngx/mcp@0.3.0"] }
  }
}
\`\`\`

Docs: https://cngxjs.github.io/cngx/
"
`;
